<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santa Fe, New Mexico</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1610">1610</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Santa Fe was founded around 1610 by the Spanish governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-peralta">Pedro de Peralta</a> as the capital of the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-mexico">New Mexico</a>, on the northern frontier of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a>. Pueblo rebels drove the Spanish out in 1680, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diego-de-vargas">Diego de Vargas</a> reoccupied it in 1692. It remained the capital under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> and then the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santa-fe-new-mexico.jpg" alt="Santa Fe, New Mexico" width="320" height="146" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tony Hisgett from Birmingham, UK · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Palace_of_the_Governors.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
